questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput Spring Boot service experiences gradual Old Generation memory accumulation and eventual `java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space` failures after running for several days. A junior developer implemented the following payload caching mechanism to optimize async processing:

java
@Service
public class EventProcessingService {
    private static final ThreadLocal<byte[]> PAYLOAD_BUFFER = 
        ThreadLocal.withInitial(() -> new byte[10 * 1024 * 1024]); // 10MB buffer

    @Async("taskExecutor")
    public CompletableFuture<ProcessResult> processEvent(Event event) {
        byte[] buffer = PAYLOAD_BUFFER.get();
        System.arraycopy(event.getRawBytes(), 0, buffer, 0, event.getRawBytes().length);
        ProcessResult result = parseAndExecute(buffer);
        return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(result);
    }
}


The `taskExecutor` bean is configured as a `ThreadPoolTaskExecutor` with a fixed pool of 50 worker threads.
